 ### Voxel Annihilation
-Voxel Annihilation removes all solid voxels from the entire SVO grid, used when a hit's effective power is overwhelmingly larger than the object's hp [S3, unofficial]. It iterates through all grid indices $(x, y, z)$ from 0 to `grid_dim`. If the voxel at $(x, y, z)$ is solid, it is removed from the SVO, its world position is calculated, and it is added to `gib_positions` [S3, unofficial]. After the loop, `solid_count` is set to 0 and `dirty` is set to true [S3, unofficial].
