 ## Background
-Sphere Carving is a fundamental voxel operation used in voxel-based games and simulations for destructible environments. It is implemented in engines like Prometheus Engine for handling object destruction [S3, unofficial] and in voxel terrain systems like dVoxels for cave generation and player interaction [S1, unofficial]. The method is distinct from the "Sphere Carving" algorithm for bounding volume generation for SDFs [S2], which uses a similar name but serves a different purpose (computing bounding proxies for acceleration). In the context of voxel occupancy, it is a direct application of the 3D filled circle kernel logic to modify grid state.
